7. Injured Smt. Kasturi Devi examined as PW-1 has inter alia deposed about - (i) bodily injuries suffered in road traffic accident near Tokas Mall, Ambarhai Village, Sector-19, Dwarka, New Delhi on 21.03.2017 at about 7:35 pm after she was hit by Motorcycle No. TN-56J-5858 coming from the side of Pocket-2 at very high speed in rash and negligent manner; (ii) treatment at Ayushman Hospital, Sector-12, Ashirwad Chowk, Dwarka, New Delhi & Ortho Plus Hospital, Gopal Nagar,
Najafgarh; (iii) expenses incurred on treatment, medicines, conveyance, attendant & special diet;
(iv) monthly income Rs.10,000/- to Rs.15,000/- by sewing/stitching clothes AND (v) general and special damages consequent to bodily injury suffered in road accident.

She has also relied upon following documents:
i. DAR - Ex.PW-1/1 ;
Kashturi Devi vs Sakthi Sr on 6 June, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/181990224/
4 ii. Copy of Disability Certificate assessing Temporary Physical Disability of 30% w.r.t.
Left Upper Limb which could improve with Physiotherapy - Ex.PW-1/2; iii. Copy of Adhar Card - Ex.PW-1/3;
iv. Treatment Record of Ortho Plus Hospital & Ayushman Hospital - Ex.PW-1/4 (Colly.);
v. Discharge Summary of Ortho Plus Hospital - Ex.PW-1/5.
8. PW-2 Dr. Vinal Sharma, CMO, Orthopaedic Department, DDU Hospital, Hari Nagar, New Delhi has deposed about Temporary Physical Disability of 30% w.r.t.

(ii) Loss of earnings (and other gains) which the injured would have made had he not been injured, comprising :
(a) Loss of earning during the period of treatment;
(b) Loss of future earnings on account of permanent disability.

Following factors are to be taken into account for assessing compensation under the head - Pain and Suffering:
i. Nature of injury;
ii. Parts of body where injuries occurred; iii. Surgeries, if any;
iv. Confinement in hospital;
v. Duration of the treatment.
